<div id="S5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o progressive exploration.</span>
Removing the forced-to-free schedule causes a larger average drop, from 61.4% to
55.6%, with particularly large decreases on Code (9.6 points) and Reason (8.4
points). More strikingly, the learned policy collapses entirely to single-round
execution (1.00/.00/.00). This supports the role of progressive exploration in
maintaining cross-mode exploration before fully autonomous mode selection.
Notably, both ablated variants (58.8% and 55.6%) still exceed the strongest fixed-paradigm baseline (55.3%, Router-R1).</p>
</div>
