<td id="A1.T4.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;">Router</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each Worker receives the sub-query written in its <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">route</span> element together
with the mode-specific context described below. A trajectory must follow the
grammar and the execution constraints of its mode:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Single-round:</span> exactly one call
<span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;route model="<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>"&gt;<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>&lt;/route&gt;</span>,
followed by the final answer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-round:</span> two to four sequential calls of the same form, one per
router turn; each call after the first also receives the previous observation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Agentic:</span> calls of the form
<br class="ltx_break"> <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;route model="<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>" role="<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>" refs="<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>"&gt;<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>&lt;/route&gt;</span>,
<br class="ltx_break">with <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r\in\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{</annotation></semantics></math>planner, executor, verifier, summarizer<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> a
comma-separated list of node IDs (empty for the first layer). Several routes in one
router turn form a layer and run in parallel; a route may reference only outputs of
earlier layers, which the environment inserts into that Worker’s input. Each output
returns as <span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;observation id="n<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>" role="<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>"&gt;</span>. At most
eight Worker calls and ten router action turns are allowed.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The first action that violates the grammar or an execution constraint of the mode
terminates the trajectory with rewards <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1,-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1,-1)</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS1" title="C.1 Rewards and Cost Accounting ‣ Appendix C Training Details ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
