<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation data.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluation uses 1,060 test questions that do not overlap with the training
questions: 120 each from MATH, Omni-MATH, APPS, LiveCodeBench, SuperGPQA, SATBench,
TriviaQA, and SimpleQA-Verified, and 100 from TACO.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Evaluation Protocol</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Per-dataset scoring.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Every question receives a binary score, and we report accuracy per dataset.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MATH, Omni-MATH:</span> symbolic mathematical equivalence with the
reference answer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">APPS:</span> the extracted program is executed in a sandbox on standard
input and is correct if its output matches on all test cases.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LiveCodeBench, TACO:</span> extracted code is executed and is correct
if it passes all retained test cases. At most 40 test cases are kept per problem;
for LiveCodeBench, test cases are additionally kept in their original order only
while their cumulative serialized size stays within 256 KB (at least one is
always kept). Both rules are deterministic, so the full official test suites are
not always used.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SuperGPQA:</span> the last option letter in the response must match
the reference exactly.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SATBench:</span> the last occurrence of SAT or UNSAT in the response must
match the reference label.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SimpleQA-Verified:</span> normalized exact match, or the reference
answer appears in the response as a whole-word match.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TriviaQA:</span> exact match with any reference alias after SQuAD-style
normalization (lowercasing and removing punctuation, articles, and extra
whitespace).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Aggregation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Domain accuracy is the unweighted mean of the accuracies of its constituent datasets,
and Avg is the unweighted mean of the five domain accuracies.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Router and Worker Models</h3>

<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Router.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507, with full-parameter fine-tuning. The KL reference policy is
the frozen initial router. Only the router is trained.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Workers.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The six Workers are frozen and are exposed to the router under fixed anonymous IDs.
The router’s system prompt lists each ID with a fixed capability description
(Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Workers. ‣ B.3 Router and Worker Models ‣ Appendix B Experimental Setup ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) and never contains model names or prices. worker_1 and
worker_2 are deployed locally on two NVIDIA A100 GPUs, and worker_3 to worker_6 are
accessed through OpenRouter; the serving setup is the same in training and
evaluation.</p>
</div>
