<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Training Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Rewards and Cost Accounting</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section completes the definitions of Section <a href="#S4" title="4 RouteWeaver ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rewards and excluded rollouts.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each trajectory receives the two rewards of Eq. <a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4.1 Unified Trajectory Representation and Execution ‣ 4 RouteWeaver ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Correctness is judged
by the dataset-specific scorers of Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Evaluation Protocol ‣ Appendix B Experimental Setup ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>. The first action that
violates the grammar
or an execution constraint of the mode (Appendix <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Action Format ‣ Appendix A Routing Interface ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) terminates
the trajectory, which receives <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1,-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1,-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, remains in <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, and enters the
group statistics like any other rollout. A rollout affected by an infrastructure
failure, such as a Worker call returning no response, is not attributed to the router
and is not treated as terminal-invalid; it is excluded from <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence
from all group statistics, the policy loss, and the KL term. When the efficiency reward is enabled
(<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>), trajectories with incomplete cost records are excluded from
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> in the same way, so they enter neither reward component nor the
corresponding updates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cost measure.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> sums the inference cost of every Worker call in <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, computed from the
call’s input and output tokens at the fixed reference prices of
Table <a href="#A3.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Cost measure. ‣ C.1 Rewards and Cost Accounting ‣ Appendix C Training Details ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> (in USD per million tokens). The same frozen table is used for
the efficiency reward and for all reported costs. These prices serve only to measure
Worker inference cost; they are not the amounts actually paid, and the router’s own
cost is not included. The normalization constant <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathrm{ref}}=0.0070716653" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0070716653</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathrm{ref}}=0.0070716653</annotation></semantics></math>
USD is the 95th percentile of the per-trajectory Worker cost over 1,024 rollouts
(128 training queries, 8 rollouts each) sampled from the step-25 cold-start
checkpoint with the training decoding settings, excluding only infrastructure failures
and trajectories with incomplete usage records. It is frozen for all runs, so that
<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathrm{cost}}(\tau)=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>cost</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathrm{cost}}(\tau)=1/2</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\tau)=C_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\tau)=C_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
