<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Component-wise group statistics.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a reward component <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\{\mathrm{task},\mathrm{eff}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>task</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>eff</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\{\mathrm{task},\mathrm{eff}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with values <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i,c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i,c}</annotation></semantics></math>, a
group with retained rollouts <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> and mode subsets <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> has</p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{V}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{V}}r_{i,c},\qquad\mu_{m,c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{V}_{m}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{V}_{m}}r_{i,c},\qquad\sigma_{c}=\operatorname{std}\big(\{r_{i,c}\}_{i\in\mathcal{V}}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{V}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{V}}r_{i,c},\qquad\mu_{m,c}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{V}_{m}|}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{V}_{m}}r_{i,c},\qquad\sigma_{c}=\operatorname{std}\big(\{r_{i,c}\}_{i\in\mathcal{V}}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and advantages</p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}=\frac{r_{i,c}-\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{c}+\epsilon},\qquad A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{mode}}=\frac{\mu_{m_{i},c}-\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{c}+\epsilon},\qquad A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{inner}}=\frac{r_{i,c}-\mu_{m_{i},c}}{\sigma_{c}+\epsilon}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>GRPO</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>mode</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>inner</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}=\frac{r_{i,c}-\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{c}+\epsilon},\qquad A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{mode}}=\frac{\mu_{m_{i},c}-\mu_{c}}{\sigma_{c}+\epsilon},\qquad A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{inner}}=\frac{r_{i,c}-\mu_{m_{i},c}}{\sigma_{c}+\epsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sample (Bessel-corrected) standard deviation over all retained
rollouts of the group, not a per-mode one, and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The advantages used in training mix the components with the run’s fixed weight
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{l}=(1-\alpha)\,A_{i,\mathrm{task}}^{l}+\alpha\,A_{i,\mathrm{eff}}^{l},\qquad l\in\{\mathrm{GRPO},\mathrm{mode},\mathrm{inner}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>task</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>eff</mi></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>GRPO</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>mode</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>inner</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{l}=(1-\alpha)\,A_{i,\mathrm{task}}^{l}+\alpha\,A_{i,\mathrm{eff}}^{l},\qquad l\in\{\mathrm{GRPO},\mathrm{mode},\mathrm{inner}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which extends Eq. <a href="#S4.E7" title="In 4.2 COMET-GRPO ‣ 4 RouteWeaver ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> to the ordinary GRPO advantage used by forced
groups. Each component is normalized by its own group statistics before mixing; the
rewards are never combined into a scalar and normalized jointly, and no further
batch-level normalization or whitening is applied.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Component-wise gating.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each component is gated separately: if <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{c}&lt;10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{c}&lt;10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, component <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>
contributes no advantage for that group. A group whose rollouts are all correct but
differ in cost therefore keeps its efficiency signal when <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, although its
task signal is gated. A group whose rollouts are all excluded from <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>
contributes no gradient.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ordinary GRPO loss.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}=S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}}\cup S_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>mode</mi></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>inner</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}=S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}}\cup S_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{pol}}=\sum_{i}|S_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>pol</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{pol}}=\sum_{i}|S_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}^{\mathrm{global}}=\frac{1}{N_{\mathrm{pol}}}\sum_{i}\sum_{k\in S_{i}}\ell_{ik}(A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>GRPO</mi><mi>global</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>pol</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{GRPO}}^{\mathrm{global}}=\frac{1}{N_{\mathrm{pol}}}\sum_{i}\sum_{k\in S_{i}}\ell_{ik}(A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In cold start every mode prefix is injected, so <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>mode</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> contains only execution tokens, and only the task component is used,
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}=A_{i,\mathrm{task}}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>task</mi></mrow><mi>GRPO</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}=A_{i,\mathrm{task}}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dual clipping.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For negative advantages, the token loss of Eq. <a href="#S4.E8" title="In 4.2 COMET-GRPO ‣ 4 RouteWeaver ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> is additionally
bounded as <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{ik}(A)\leftarrow\min\{\ell_{ik}(A),-cA\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{ik}(A)\leftarrow\min\{\ell_{ik}(A),-cA\}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, with
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=3</annotation></semantics></math>, which limits the loss of a negative-advantage token whose ratio has grown
large. The clipping ranges are <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{-}=\eta_{+}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{-}=\eta_{+}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">KL regularization.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S4.E10" title="In 4.2 COMET-GRPO ‣ 4 RouteWeaver ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> is computed against the frozen initial
router, the original Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 rather than the cold-start checkpoint,
with coefficient <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (Appendix <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Hyperparameters and Decoding ‣ Appendix C Training Details ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>); <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{ik}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{ik}</annotation></semantics></math> is the low-variance
(<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>) estimator, and the KL term enters the loss rather than the reward. It is
normalized by its own token count <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math>, not by
the segment counts of Eq. <a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.2 COMET-GRPO ‣ 4 RouteWeaver ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\mathrm{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\mathrm{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> uses the same
router-token mask as the policy loss, so rollouts excluded from <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> by
infrastructure failures are removed from both.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mixed-batch token advantages.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During the transition, the token advantage used in Eq. <a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.2 COMET-GRPO ‣ 4 RouteWeaver ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> is</p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{ik}=\begin{cases}A_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}},&amp;k\in S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}},\ \text{free group},\\[2.0pt]
A_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}},&amp;k\in S_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}},\ \text{free group},\\[2.0pt]
A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}},&amp;k\in S_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}},\ \text{forced group},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>mode</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>mode</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>free group</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>inner</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>inner</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>free group</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>inner</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mtext>forced group</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{ik}=\begin{cases}A_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}},&amp;k\in S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}},\ \text{free group},\\[2.0pt]
A_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}},&amp;k\in S_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}},\ \text{free group},\\[2.0pt]
A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}},&amp;k\in S_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}},\ \text{forced group},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where all advantages are the <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-mixed values of Eq. <a href="#A3.E16" title="In Component-wise group statistics. ‣ C.2 Optimization Details ‣ Appendix C Training Details ‣ RouteWeaver: Weaving Mode Selection and Execution into Unified LLM Routing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>. A
group is either entirely forced or entirely free. For forced groups the injected mode
tokens are masked, so <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>mode</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{\mathrm{mode}}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> and the execution tokens
receive <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>GRPO</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which equals <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>inner</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{\mathrm{inner}}</annotation></semantics></math> because all rollouts
of the group share one mode; these tokens count toward <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{inner}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>inner</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{inner}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Support-term scores.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\theta}(m,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\theta}(m,x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the summed log probability of the content tokens of candidate
mode <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> for query <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. The scores are normalized per query and averaged over the set
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> of unique queries in the batch:</p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{\theta}(m\mid x)=\frac{\exp s_{\theta}(m,x)}{\sum_{m^{\prime}\in\mathcal{M}}\exp s_{\theta}(m^{\prime},x)},\qquad\bar{p}_{m}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{U}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{U}}\tilde{p}_{\theta}(m\mid x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{\theta}(m\mid x)=\frac{\exp s_{\theta}(m,x)}{\sum_{m^{\prime}\in\mathcal{M}}\exp s_{\theta}(m^{\prime},x)},\qquad\bar{p}_{m}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{U}|}\sum_{x\in\mathcal{U}}\tilde{p}_{\theta}(m\mid x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is thus an average of normalized candidate-mode scores, not the frequency
with which <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled, and the support term does not ensure that every mode is
sampled in every batch.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Degenerate groups.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each component, if a mode has only one retained rollout, then
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m_{i},c}=r_{i,c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m_{i},c}=r_{i,c}</annotation></semantics></math> and that rollout’s inner advantage is zero; if all retained
rollouts select the same mode, then <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{m_{i},c}=\mu_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{m_{i},c}=\mu_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and all mode advantages are
zero. Gating is described above.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Relation to GRPO advantages.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each component,
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{mode}}+A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{inner}}=A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>mode</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>inner</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>GRPO</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{mode}}+A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{inner}}=A_{i,c}^{\mathrm{GRPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the
same identity holds for the mixed advantages. The mode and inner advantages supervise
disjoint token sets with separate normalization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Hyperparameters and Decoding</h3>

<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a batch size of 32 queries, 8 rollouts per query, a learning rate of
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, a KL coefficient of 0.001 against the frozen initial router, and zero
entropy regularization. Each run, for <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0,0.1,0.3,0.5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0,0.1,0.3,0.5\}</annotation></semantics></math>, starts
independently from the same initial router at step 0, is trained for 90 steps, and is
evaluated at its final checkpoint. Steps 1–25 form the cold-start phase: forced modes, standard GRPO on the
task reward with the standard-deviation gate, global token reduction, and no support
term. After step 25 each run continues its own training trajectory, enabling the
mode/inner decomposition and segment-wise reduction and mixing the task and efficiency
advantages with its fixed <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>; the KL reference remains the frozen initial
router. The forced ratio <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> decreases linearly from 1 at data batch index 25 to
0 at batch index 75, and the support coefficient is <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.002\,\rho_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.002</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.002\,\rho_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>. The support floor is <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{0}=0.002" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{0}=0.002</annotation></semantics></math>,
the clipping ranges are <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{-}=\eta_{+}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{-}=\eta_{+}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, and dual clipping uses <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=3</annotation></semantics></math>.
The optimizer is AdamW with <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=(0.9,0.999)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.999</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=(0.9,0.999)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-8}</annotation></semantics></math>, and weight
decay 0.01, using a constant learning rate without warmup or decay and global
gradient-norm clipping at 1.0. Each step performs a single on-policy update over all
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 8=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 8=256</annotation></semantics></math> trajectories of the batch, so <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{old}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the policy
that generated them. In the ablation without progressive exploration, <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{b}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{b}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for
all <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, so the support term (<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{b}=\lambda_{0}\rho_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{b}=\lambda_{0}\rho_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>) is inactive as well.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decoding.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Router, training: temperature 0.8, top-<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> 0.95, top-<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> disabled. Router, testing:
greedy decoding. Workers, training and testing: temperature 0.2, at most 4,096
output tokens; top-<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and top-<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> are not set and follow provider defaults. Worker
requests carry a fixed seed (42), which providers may ignore, and disable
thinking/reasoning modes. Because Workers sample, system-level evaluation is not fully
deterministic. Each evaluation question receives one system rollout.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Call budgets and lengths.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Identical in training and evaluation. Single-round: exactly one Worker call.
Multi-round: two to four sequential calls. Agentic: at most eight Worker calls and at
most ten router action turns. Prompts are
limited to 6,144 tokens, the multi-turn response budget to 12,288 tokens, the
mode-declaration turn to 64 tokens, and each observation to 2,048 tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
